---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="About Us - Editorial Profile" 
  description="Learn about Bijak Technology, an independent technology journal covering cloud infrastructure, enterprise ERP, and digital innovation."
  lang="en"
  alternateId="/about/"
  alternateEn="/en/about/"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-10 py-4">
    
    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="text-center py-6 border-b border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight uppercase">
        About Bijak Technology
      </h1>
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 mt-2 font-mono">
        "Because together, Everything is possible"
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Editorial Overview -->
    <div class="space-y-6 text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg">
      <p class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-extrabold first-letter:float-left first-letter:mr-3 first-letter:text-rose-600 font-medium">
        Bijak Technology was founded with a steadfast commitment to explore, evaluate, and implement cutting-edge digital technologies. We view software engineering and cloud infrastructure not as abstract jargon, but as concrete levers for solving operational, financial, and logistical bottlenecks.
      </p>
      
      <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        Through this independent publication platform, our editorial desk analyzes enterprise system architectures, open-source Frappe & ERPNext v16 implementations, containerized AI workflows, high-performance cloud VPS benchmarks, and grassroots retail logistics.
      </p>

      <p class="text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
        Our engineering contributors operate with a hands-on ethos—validating technical hypotheses directly in production code, telemetry collectors, and automated deployment pipelines.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Pillars of Competency -->
    <div class="border-t border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 pt-8 space-y-6">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-950 dark:text-white uppercase tracking-tight text-center">
        Core Editorial Pillars
      </h2>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400 bg-rose-100/70 dark:bg-rose-950/40 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md inline-block">Pillar 1</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Cloud Infrastructure & High-Performance VPS</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Practical blueprints for deploying containerized services, reverse proxies, and database clusters on self-managed KVM virtual private servers with uncompromising IOPS and uptime.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400 bg-rose-100/70 dark:bg-rose-950/40 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md inline-block">Pillar 2</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Enterprise ERP & Data Sovereignty</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            In-depth guides on ERPNext v16, Frappe Framework, manufacturing scheduling, inventory control, and enterprise compliance on private cloud environments.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400 bg-rose-100/70 dark:bg-rose-950/40 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md inline-block">Pillar 3</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Software Architecture & System Resilience</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Authoritative discussions comparing distributed event architectures, caching hierarchies, and database scaling methodologies for modern web applications.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-slate-300/80 dark:border-slate-800 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 shadow-sm space-y-2">
          <span class="text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400 bg-rose-100/70 dark:bg-rose-950/40 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-md inline-block">Pillar 4</span>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-slate-950 dark:text-white">Smart Living & Practical Science</h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            Data-backed explorations into energy auditing, household resource budgeting, and foundational science translated into tangible lifestyle efficiency.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</Layout>
